  "repair_or_experiment_note": "# E1 persistent retention regression: rollback and bounded G1 repair\n\nThe human requested repair now. Both original G0 stable blocks have naturally ended with complete own saves and uniquely settled canonical segments. Their training integrity was healthy, but their independent old-skill behavior was not. Block2 model32988 SHA1989ee12ba947e695dc42e80e1f9f07a627c2b5a488f88814552ec3a16559130 made468updates/224640000environment steps/44928callbacks and its original parent settled7228.0752795s once. It had no ordinary training event/nonfinite/integrity STOP, closure0.90584mm. We do not change its original health or costs.\n\nFour existing3060 cases were completed and independently reviewed, with8 returned probe/result JSON byte hashes and the full184021639byte terrain NPZ SHAca0e611741ba72a80e912122372a5be245de3cb77d8eb502c827952c106ea16f. Full pre-reset signed route progress excludes reset teleportation; actual ground/contact-force integration/COMlink/target callbacks/reasons use original tolerances. Terrain forward0.29301/reverse-0.29263m/s remained useful, ordinary0. However world63/64 at32053 became16/64 in block1 and14/64 in block2; block2 worst complete-circle signed cross drift0.13408m/s, negative4pi0/8 mean-11.21156rad/s and positive4pi2/8. Negative straight1.5m/s command error1.00029m/s is substantial. Flat env38 actually reset once and its original task/data admission flag is false. This failure is retained, not changed into a pass. The flat evaluation does not contain a complete raw failure trajectory; retained per-environment/failure group facts and changed DR rows are the available evidence.\n\nTwo independent reader rejections are retained: an incorrect reused module path before GPU, and an invalid no-reset assumption in the strict pairing reader. The diagnostic reader preserves the false admission flag, checks only actual env38 episode+1 across managers and unaffected rows exactly, and pairs initial root30q/parameters/recipes/assignments. Neither reader rejection was a production GPU/PPO failure.\n\nRollback source is earlier complete, behavior-reviewed E1 model32053 SHA655a36b78926bc17d4230996fe152b62d0f997f3037105d5247582697440481f, with actor/critic/std/optimizer/D1-D7/globalCPUCUDA/named streams and E1 bookkeeping. It has useful terrain behavior and much better inherited skills, with original small negative4pi/world boundary residuals preserved. We do not select maxiter/preflight/unreviewed32988 as the new source and do not touch frozen E0.\n\nNew isolated root is /home/egde/rl_candidates/MOD4_S3_E1_G1_REPAIR_20261009:313 original files unchanged plus8 newfiles=321. Under human003 revision, only the original random-height terrain family is replaced by a CAD-derived10mm peak-to-trough continuous wave, mean local period0.24064192875m and10-wave section2.406422727m. Flat joins/10mm scaling and flat local datum are explicitly derived training geometry, not real RM70mm or the outer-island curb. The original finite mesh/BRep section error about1.4373mm is preserved. Other four family configurations and existing proportions,35actor/38cleancritic/6actions,2.5msx4/TGS32-4,20kx24/LR1e-4 adaptive/save25/KEEP_STD1, allD0-D7 and hardware/health/contact data tolerances stay fixed. This is not the rejected70/20/10quota scheme, a teacher, new reward or new LR.\n\nInitial G0->G1 explicitly restores old E1 bookkeeping and all D1-D7/optimizer/globalnamed streams, verifies actualCUDA state roundtrip, then creates one new physical episode on the new mesh. It never claims exact restoration of the old mesh/PhysX state into a new terrain. Same-G1 later restoration requires identical mesh/profile and complete E1 state. Actual targetCPU14schema tests and independent geometry ray/formula tests passed. New geometry requires its own10env300control SDK,20k24warmup+120timed native,128x2/20kx4 fullPPO discard scopes once; old clock/DR math scope is reused. CPU/native/frozen no-PPO work is not charged, completePPO load/learn/save/exit is uniquely charged under the same canonical230h total, budget added0.\n\nActual recorded phase at 1791561757.1303353: bounded_E1_G1_retention_repair_learning. Parent/guardian/child and own receipts are in the actual snapshot; results absent there are pending. The first formal observation is limited to900s, followed automatically by one newG1 terrain case plus exact-old-package flat/spin/world candidate cases and a saved-review boundary. A separate32053 anchor is evaluated on the newG1 mesh; oldG0 terrain evidence cannot admit this new geometry. No further G1 PPO is automatic before complete behavior review. Full entry-to-exit crossing and old-skill recovery are not claimed before the actual trajectory review.\n\nThis rollback and shortened observation contain wasted repeated narrow training while advancing003 one geometry axis. Persistent forgetting is consistent with narrow adaptation, but there is no causal ablation or proven permanent cure. RM001 valid spin exclusions and002 actual outer-curb clarification remain; optional93/94 and MuJoCo remain paused, S8/gate are not newly approved/trained. All raw/false/weights/costs are retained and all saved stage reports, errors, implementation and sync receipts are captured in Git; large binaries are indexed only.\n",
